  B: { name: 'Goblin munitions', desc: 'The whole machine as goblin munitions: a scorched gunmetal panel with a green paint stripe, rivets and a hazard band at the recipe end; chalk stencils for the empty slots; rusty bronze and gunmetal cogs. The drum is a fluted revolver cylinder with brass-rimmed chambers, and it puffs powder smoke as it clacks round. Green trolley with hazard tape, steel arm with green joints; lining up flashes green.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, GOB139); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  C: { name: 'Drum rides the front', desc: 'Redesign: no arm and no magazine at the start. The revolver drum is the front of the bar and rolls along a brass rail like a wheel. Each skill-up it rolls forward one slot and leaves the cog from its bottom chamber behind (the cog opens out to full size in the mesh): KA-THUNK, the train turns. The finished train trails behind it on a dark walnut panel; engraved outlines show the slots ahead.',
    draw(I, y, t) { drumFront140(I, y, t); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  D: { name: 'Open girder, hanging cogs', desc: 'Redesign: no case at all. A riveted steel I-beam runs above the bar (hazard-striped end) and every cog hangs from it on its own hanger; empty hangers end in an open hook. The drum hangs from the beam’s start like a winch, the trolley runs under the beam and the arm carries each cog out to its hook. Open air, goblin industrial.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, GIR140); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  E: { name: 'Two-row gearbox', desc: 'Redesign: the cogs sit in two staggered rows, upper and lower, each meshing with the one before and after like a real gearbox, so the bar holds up to 24 smaller cogs: denser and taller. The drum feeds from the start and the arm sets each cog into its row on the blueprint.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, TWO140); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  F: { name: 'Big drum is the counter', desc: 'Redesign: a big gunmetal revolver drum at the start is the main piece; its 8 chambers hold the cogs still to come, and its toothed rim drives a short chain of up to 11 big cogs. Each skill-up the chambers clunk round, the drum FIRES the next cog down the line (muzzle puff, a streak), and it slams into the chain: KA-THUNK, the drum and chain turn together. Goblin.',
    draw(I, y, t) { bigDrum140(I, y, t); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
// round 140 entries C-F (moved out in round 141)
// round 141 entries (A-F) replaced in round 142 by the combined A
  A: { name: 'Revolver drum', desc: 'The blueprint gear train with the revolver-drum magazine: a round brass drum at the start with six chambers, a small cog in each one still to come. The arm pulls the cog out of the chamber facing the bar and it grows to full size, the drum clunks round one chamber and a latch clicks; the cog is carried over and pressed into its drawing, KA-THUNK, the train turns.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, RV138); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  B: { name: 'Clean: one housing', desc: 'Cleanup idea: the drum moves inside the case (the cog row starts after it), and one brass-framed, pill-shaped housing holds everything: the drum sits in its own brass bezel at the left end, and the trolley runs on a rail built into the inside of the frame, so nothing pokes out of the case or into the header.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, CLB141); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  C: { name: 'Clean: calm', desc: 'Cleanup idea: same layout as A with the visual noise taken out: no grid, no glass shine, no depth shadows; one brass family for the cogs; empty slots are quiet dotted circles with a centre dot; a thin hairline frame; softer glows; a smaller trolley.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, CLC141); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  D: { name: 'Clean: instrument panel', desc: 'Cleanup idea: the whole module is one instrument: a dark riveted plate with a brass bezel holds the header, the bar and the recipe line; the cog row sits in a recessed channel, the drum is set into the plate as a dial with its own bezel, and the trolley rides a brass rail across the plate above the channel.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, CLD141); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  E: { name: '>15: inked in steps', desc: 'For gaps over 15 (switch to the 50-point gap): each cog stands for 3-4 points; each point inks one wedge of the next drawing into metal (a tick and a spark, divider marks show the steps). The arm waits by the drum holding the next cog and only carries it over and presses it in when the last wedge fills. The drum only turns when a cog leaves it.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, INK141); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
  F: { name: '>15: small cogs merge', desc: 'For gaps over 15 (switch to the 50-point gap): every point the drum turns and fires a small cog into the next slot, where it sits in a little ring; when the slot’s small cogs are all in, they pull together into one big cog with a flash and the KA-THUNK, and the train turns. No arm here: the drum does the work, so it turns every point because it fires something every point.',
    draw(I, y, t) { fetch136(I, y, t, MRG141); }, snd(o, v, n) { gsnd133(o, v, n); } },
